Hold-loop USB service for a held boot. NOT applied, NOT built, NOT tested on the board.

Why: in a boot held by the entry-hold gate (safe mode arms it automatically), CPU1 stays parked in
vcpu1_run(), and the MUSB gadget is serviced from CPU1's IRQ path, so the USB console never enumerates
(host: error -71) for that whole boot; soak72 then refuses to start (board-off-usb). See HANDOFF.md,
2026-09-30, "Open: no USB console in a boot that was held".

Why it is not applied: usbacm.h warns that usbacm_poll() is the only code besides musb_init() that drives
these registers and that CPU1's poll drives the same ones, so calling it from CPU0 needs a check that CPU1
is really parked at that point. Apply against main_dbg.c at 5fd522f or later, build with `make hv-uimage`,
test with a held boot (safe mode), and only then commit it into main_dbg.c.

--- a/main_dbg.c	2026-10-05 20:52:04.677370911 +0300
+++ b/main_dbg.c	2026-10-10 04:21:28.851784495 +0300
@@ -715,6 +715,11 @@
 			wdt_debug_kick();
 			if (!dbg_core_active)
 				dbgmon_service(&g_last_guest_frame);
+			/* Service the MUSB gadget while held: without this the USB
+			 * console never enumerates in a held boot (HANDOFF 2026-09-30,
+			 * host sees error -71) and soak72 refuses to start
+			 * (board-off-usb). */
+			usbacm_poll();
 			if (dbgtools_release_get())
 				break;
 		}
